Replication Steps
1-Build or modify the printer frame.
2-Install the syringe extrusion mount.
3-Assemble the pneumatic system.
4-Wire the Arduino Nano controller.
5-Connect the ADS1115, MCP4725, LCD, relays, and sensors.
6-Update printer and Arduino Firmware.
7-Calibrate the pressure sensors.
Test solenoid operation.
Run low-pressure extrusion tests.


See Readme.md for required components

1-Assemble printer
  -Ensure printer function as intended without any modifications
  -Confirm that all motion Axis move correctly
  -Remove filament extruder copenents such as extruder motor and hotend
    -In the case of the Sovol SV08 the extruder conteol board will need to be kept along with eddy current probe
  -Modify Klipper firmware and remove(comment) control over hotend,hotplate and extruder motor to avoid errors while printing
  - Test printing without extrusion components, make sure no errors occur start to finish

2-Install Syringe Mount
  -Using stl file 3d print a new mount for 10mL syringe and eddy current probe
  -New mount will remain on the same printer carriage
  -Connect pneumatic tubing to using barrel adapter
